  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4602.23 CO2 budget emissions limitation",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4602.23 “CO2 budget emissions limitation” means, for a CO2 budget source, the number of allowances held by the CO2 budget source in a compliance account at the end of a control period or an interim control period equivalent to the tons of CO2 emissions in that control period or an interim control period.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09; ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14 (from Env-A 4602.21); ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20 (from Env-A 4602.24)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4600.html"
